  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-180220",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we express the fraction as a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}x=\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $\\frac{4}{7},$ which is \n\n$$\n{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{-1}=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nThis gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{7}x & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{7}x & =\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1x & =\\frac{14}{12} \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
